	abstract = {Transcranial magnetic pulse stimulation ({TMS}) over the region of the sensorimotor cortex impairs both perception and tactile localization of cutaneous stimuli delivered to the fingers of the contralateral hand. The region of the scalp over which {TMS} results in impaired cutaneous localization coincides with the region over which {TMS} suppresses simple perception. {TMS} has a more profound effect on tactile localization than on simple detection of cutaneous stimuli. {TMS} disrupts tactile localization for 400 ms after tactile perception has returned to normal.},
